I explored what logistics companies need from a profitability tracking and reporting tool, and helped shape its first version around real customer insight. The project owner had already created a preliminary version of the tool. My task, together with my teammate, was to find out what transport industry customers needed and how much demand there was for the tool.

We drafted a rough schedule and project plan, prepared an interview guide, looked for suitable interviewees and invited them to take part. We contacted eight CEOs and transport managers at transport companies by email and phone, and one agreed to an interview. That one interview gave us rich, useful answers and let us move the tool forward.

The interview was built around three main topics, which we explored with specific questions in a semi-structured format. We recorded the interview, then anonymized, transcribed and summarized it using AI tools. Based on what we learned, we built a visual prototype of the product and prepared sales materials so the tool can be taken to customers.
